    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe change is well-placed overall: `generateCustomerCode` stays in the service where the sequence/repository access belongs, and because `membershipNumber` is derived by simply formatting `<customerCode>-M<YY>` in `OwnerMapper`, it correctly rebuilds on the new format automatically with only a doc-example update \u2014 no logic duplication across the two units. One structural issue:\n\n**Duplicated \"first three letters, upper-cased\" extraction in `generateCustomerCode` (ClinicServiceImpl.java:256-259).** The spec defines CITY3 and LAST3 as the exact same operation, and the code now expresses that operation twice verbatim:\n\n```java\nString city = owner.getCity() == null ? \"\" : owner.getCity();\nString city3 = city.substring(0, Math.min(3, city.length())).toUpperCase();\nString lastName = owner.getLastName() == null ? \"\" : owner.getLastName();\nString last3 = lastName.substring(0, Math.min(3, lastName.length())).toUpperCase();\n```\n\nThe non-trivial null-guard + `substring(0, Math.min(3, len))` + `toUpperCase()` expression is repeated. Extract a small private helper that names the shared rule, e.g.:\n\n```java\nprivate static String prefix3(String value) {\n    String s = value == null ? \"\" : value;\n    return s.substring(0, Math.min(3, s.length())).toUpperCase();\n}\n```\n\nThen the method body becomes `prefix3(owner.getCity())` / `prefix3(owner.getLastName())`, removing the duplication and making the two identically-derived prefixes read as one concept. (Note the per-city `count()` filter still needs the raw `city` value for `equalsIgnoreCase`, so keep that local; only the prefix derivation is duplicated.)",
    "review_cost_usd": 0.1981,
    "fix_cost_usd": 1.0265,
